<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">French East India Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1664</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> was a chartered trading company founded in 1664 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>'s minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-colbert">Colbert</a>. It established posts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pondicherry">Pondicherry</a>, and competed with the British East India Company, but lost out in the wars of the mid-eighteenth century, limiting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>'s role in India.</p></div>
